<title>UK: July Forties programme set higher at 22.4 mln bbls.</title>
<headline>July Forties programme set higher at 22.4 mln bbls.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>July's U.K. North Sea Forties programme schedules liftings totalling 22.4 million barrels, up from a revised 16.8 million in June, traders said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The difference, 5.6 million barrels, is the equivalent of 11.2 standard 500,000-barrel cargoes more than the revised June programme.</p>
<p>The July programme is made up of 26 cargoes of 500,000 barrels, 11 of 600,000 barrels, and one each of 700,000 barrels, 650,000 barrels and 450,000 barrels with a further one million barrels which will go direct to Forties pipeline operator BP's refinery at Grangemouth.</p>
</text>
